# Reference SGML whose document element (doc) requires (a, b): only <a> is given,
# and inside it c (- O, model (m,n)) gets only <m>. Exercises the whole
# "not finished" diagnostic family, all corpus-neutral bolt-ons:
#   - elementNotFinished       ("C" not finished but containing element ended)
#                              when </a> implies the end of the still-open c
#   - elementEndTagNotFinished (end tag for "A" which is not finished)
#                              since a still needs d at its explicit </a>
#   - elementNotFinishedDocumentEnd ("DOC" not finished but document ended)
#                              since doc still needs b at end of document
#   - omitEndTagDeclare + "start tag was here" aux, since doc is `- -` and its
#                              end tag may not be omitted.
# ESIS is the fully-recovered element tree; exit 1.
BASE=entry
DOC=doc.sgm
